---
paths: "**/*.sh"
---

# Bash Scripting Standards

- `set -e` — fail fast, no silent errors
- Trust exit codes, not file existence checks
- Run the command, don't verify preconditions it already checks
- One script = one job (build, test, deploy — not all three)
- If the command succeeds, it worked — no redundant validation

